OpenNEC version history

Version 2.1.1 - 2026 June 6
- trying to fix massive regression issues
- fixed indentation on STRUCTURE EXCITATION
- fixed spacing in the TOTAL SEGMENTS USED footer

Version 2.1.0 - 2026 June 6
- the output format now defaults to "original" on all platforms, you can still override with --format (but you won't)
- added the version number to the header in reports, so it's "(onec 2.1.0)" instead of "(onec)"
- decks now store blank lines and treats them like comments, these are often seen in 4nec2 decks
- added code to detect the type of line endings and use them when writing files (reduces the need for --line-ending)
- fixed a problem when using CRLF and tab field separators that cause some files to fail to parse
- fixed issues around EX cards, correctly batches them now
- fixed a major issue in the way EX was being calculated that inverted some results
- added max(a,b) and min(a,b) functions for 4nec2 support
- added the missing "fix" function as well
- allow underscore at front of variable names (SY cards)
- added arc-trig functions
- PT cards now properly suppress the CURRENT output in those cases
- changes to the way the .out file is written so something gets sent out even with errors

Version 2.0.0 - 2026 June 2
- re-releasing 1.4.3 as 2.0.0 now that it passes 4nec2 testing!

Version 1.4.3 - 2026 May 31
- decks with CP cards but no NLs now work properly. this is not valid in NEC-2, but is in NEC-4
- more work on OpenBLAS on Windows

Version 1.4.2 - 2026 May 21
- fix grouping issues with DATA CARD listing with multiple batches using a 4nec2 frequency file
- added missing column headers in STRUCTURE EXCITATION section
- examined PIVOT debug info... do we really need that?

Version 1.4.1 - 2026 May 13
- fixed issue in radiation pattern output for small E(PHI) values
- fixed issues scaling the output values from surface patches (was an output-only issue)
- minor display issue in the way connections were displayed (PCHCON)
- added separate builds for OpenBLAS and "original" math code

Version 1.4.0 - 2026 May 11
- fixed surface patch currents output formatting

Version 1.3.9 - 2026 May 7
- work on getting patch output working

Version 1.3.8 - 2026 May 4
- more work on fortran formatting
- explored issue with first and last items in radiation pattern output, turns out we're better

Version 1.3.7 - 2026 April 26
- more work on fortran formatting

Version 1.3.4 - 2026 April 21
- lots of work getting the "original" --format to exactly match the Fortran code from the PC
- as part of that, a --line-ending switch has been added to produce "crlf" or just "lf"
--line-ending now defaults to 'lf' on Unix/macOS and 'crlf' on Windows
